        "read": false,
        "user_title": null,
        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "For most villains, more heroes make it easier. Regarding villains dealing more damage, I will copy a <a href=\"https://greaterthangames.com/comment/52024#comment-52024\">post</a> I wrote a while ago here:\n\n[quote=\"Pydro\"]\n\nI think this is a good example of the theoretical vs the practical. True, in lower H games you can nulify the damage, but does it really matter?\n\nConsider 3 heroes with 25 hp each, and an attack of H-2. Let&#39;s see how many instances of damage are needed to wipe out the team:\n\n3p game - No DR: 75 / 1 = 75 instances\n\n3p game - each with DR 1: Nullified\n\n4p game - No DR: 100 / 2 = 50\n\n4p game - each with DR 1: 100 / 1 = 100 Instances\n\n5p game - No DR: 125 / 3 = 42 instances\n\n5p game - each with DR 1: 125 / 2 = 53 instances\n\nIn each case, DR does help. Now, its true a DR of 1 can nulify the damage in a 3p game, but look how many times the heroes need to be hit before they are killed. Even in a 5p game with no DR, it would still take 42 times of being hit before being incapped. That&#39;s huge. You can often kill the villain before then, so it doesn&#39;t really matter, and villains don&#39;t play more cards based on the number of people. To compensate, you get an extra play, power and a variety of effects to help you kill the villain even faster. While it&#39;s nice to end the game at full hp, in many circumstances it simply doesn&#39;t matter, and more players make the game much easier.\n\nTrue, if you have a villain that can put out that many instances (Matty), then a 3p game will make a difference, but if they can&#39;t, a 5p game will almost always be easier. The only other instance this matter is if there is a lot of AoE damage.\n\n[/quote]\n\nI was a little bored, so I <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1jsuqgNDuxPKZd_99hkNgA_ycZzbo9WBjI1rlRYs9Guk/edit?usp=sharing\">went through the numbers</a> with an H-2, H-1, and H-0 attack.\n",
