      {
        "id": 105446,
        "name": "Humble-Knight",
        "username": "Humble-Knight",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/humble-knight/{size}/2259_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-06-02T03:02:25.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>And certain villains increase their difficulty in other ways based on H. The dreamer is much more difficult on H=4 than on H=3, and H=5 is near impossible, but that's just because you have to survive much longer, getting closer to Pydro's number. Miss Information is the same way, she requires you to take more bad cards, and she deals more instances before you're able to hit her.&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>That said, almost every other villain is easier on H=5. Voss is a great example of this. He scales with H by having more starting minions and his damage on his back side. The minions deal more instances of damage. This is why if the heroes can get past his DR, it's almost always better to leave him on his front side and beat on him there, where after you're down to 1 his damage is minimal.</p>",
        "post_number": 4,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:35:03.119Z",
